## Why This Is Asked
Understanding cross-language adapter strategies with strict latency and memory constraints.

## Key Concepts
- PEFT vs full fine-tuning in multi-language QA
- Adapter injection points (attention vs MLP)
- Language tagging vs per-language adapters
- Latency/memory budgeting and rollback plans

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo adapter injection sketch
function attachAdapters(model, keys) {
  for (const m of model.modules()) {
    if (m instanceof AttentionLayer || m instanceof MLP) {
      m.addAdapter({rank: 8, name: keys.next()});
    }
  }
  return model;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you monitor drift between languages post-deployment?
- What failure modes require bypassing adapters and using base model instead?

Why This Is Asked
This question evaluates hands-on design of a real-time RAG system, including multi-embedding chunking, multi-stage retrieval, and data freshness in production-like conditions.

Key Concepts
- Dual-embedding chunking
- Vector DB indexing and cosine search
- Cross-encoder reranking
- Streaming updates and TTL pruning
- Latency targets and observability

Code Example
```javascript
async function retrieve(query) {
  const eSent = await embed(query, 'sentence');
  const eSect = await embed(query, 'section');
  const topSent = vectorDB.search(eSent,  topK);
  const topSect = vectorDB.search(eSect, topK);
  // fuse and rerank
  return rerank(topSent, topSect, query);
}
```

Follow-up Questions
- How would you measure and improve retrieval quality in production?
- How would your design adapt if the vector DB spans multiple regions with different latencies?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests practical understanding of retrieval basics: chunking, embeddings, and vector stores in a compact, beginner‑friendly setup.

## Key Concepts
- Chunking strategy, embedding model choice, cosine similarity
- In-memory vector store for low latency
- Simple re-ranking using exact-term hits
- Latency and memory considerations in small-scale apps

## Code Example
```javascript
// Minimal pseudo-code: chunk, embed, store, search
async function chunk(text, size=400){ /* split into chunks */ }
async function embed(text){ /* call embedding API */ }
async function search(query, chunks){
  const q = await embed(query);
  const sims = chunks.map(c => ({ chunk: c, score: cosine(q, c.vec) }));
  sims.sort((a,b) => b.score - a.score);
  // simple re-ranking by term matches
  return sims.slice(0,3).sort((a,b)=>hitScore(b.chunk, query) - hitScore(a.chunk, query));
}
```

